::ENG4_U01_L04_Q01::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A modern library is no longer only a storage place for printed books. In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. What is the main idea? {
~A. Modern libraries should stop storing books.#The passage does not say this.
=B. Modern libraries function as learning centers as well as places for books.#Correct. This captures the main idea.
~C. Libraries are useful only for quiet study.#This is too narrow.
~D. Workshops are less important than printed books.#The passage does not make this comparison.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q02::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: This expanded role does not make books less important; instead, it shows that reading, research, and community learning now support one another. Which paraphrase is accurate? {
~A. The library's expanded role proves books no longer matter.#This contradicts the passage.
~B. Reading and community learning have nothing to do with each other.#This contradicts the passage.
=C. The library's new services work with books and research rather than replacing them.#Correct. This preserves the relationship.
~D. The passage says research should replace reading.#This distorts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q03::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. What does collaborative mean? {
=A. Involving people working together#Correct. Collaborative spaces support shared work.
~B. Completely silent and isolated#This is the opposite of collaborative.
~C. Printed and permanent#This is unrelated.
~D. Expensive and restricted#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q04::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Passage: When a library removes barriers to information and support, it strengthens independent learning. Which revision best improves purpose and clarity? Original: Libraries are good and help with things. {
~A. Libraries are very good and help with many good things.#This remains vague.
~B. Libraries help with things because they are helpful.#This is circular.
=C. Libraries strengthen independent learning by reducing barriers to information and support.#Correct. This revision is clear and purposeful.
~D. Libraries are good, helpful, nice, and good.#This is repetitive and vague.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q05::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. Which sentence is grammatically correct? {
~A. A strong library program balance access to texts and tools.#The singular subject needs balances.
=B. A strong library program balances access to texts and tools.#Correct. The subject and verb agree.
~C. Strong library programs balances access to texts and tools.#The plural subject needs balance.
~D. A strong library program balancing access to texts and tools.#This is a fragment.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q06::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. Which paraphrase best preserves the idea? {
=A. Libraries often support learning by offering workshops, technology, tutoring, and study areas.#Correct. This accurately restates the idea.
~B. Libraries are only useful when people need printed books.#This contradicts the passage.
~C. Libraries should not offer tutoring or technology.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. Libraries function as community stores.#This distorts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q07::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: When a library removes barriers to information and support, it strengthens independent learning. What does barriers mean here? {
~A. Decorations#This is unrelated.
=B. Obstacles#Correct. Barriers are obstacles.
~C. Bookshelves#This is too literal and incorrect.
~D. Conclusions#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q08::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. Which revision improves structure? Original: Tools are there. Texts are there. Guidance is there. This is a program. {
~A. Tools, texts, guidance, and spaces.#This is a fragment.
=B. A strong library program balances access to texts, guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces.#Correct. The revision combines related ideas into a clear structure.
~C. There are tools. There are texts. There are things.#This remains choppy and vague.
~D. Library program, access, texts, tools, guidance.#This is not a complete sentence.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q09::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: This expanded role does not make books less important; instead, it shows that reading, research, and community learning now support one another. Which student claim is best supported? {
~A. The passage rejects reading as outdated.#This contradicts the passage.
=B. The passage shows that books and broader learning services can work together.#Correct. This follows the passage's logic.
~C. The passage argues that research is unnecessary.#This contradicts the passage.
~D. The passage says community learning is separate from reading.#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q10::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: This expanded role does not make books less important; instead, it shows that reading, research, and community learning now support one another. Which punctuation mark correctly joins the two related independent clauses in the passage? {
=A. Semicolon#Correct. The semicolon joins closely related independent clauses.
~B. Apostrophe#An apostrophe does not join clauses.
~C. Question mark#The sentence is not a question.
~D. Parenthesis#Parentheses are not used to join these clauses.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q11::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. Which word is closest in meaning to guidance? {
~A. Confusion#This is the opposite.
=B. Supportive direction#Correct. Guidance means direction or support.
~C. Isolation#This is unrelated.
~D. Storage#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q12::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: When a library removes barriers to information and support, it strengthens independent learning. Which paraphrase is too vague? {
~A. Libraries can strengthen independent learning by reducing obstacles to information and support.#This is accurate.
=B. Libraries do stuff that helps people.#Correct. This is too vague for Grade 12 analysis.
~C. Removing barriers to information can help people learn independently.#This is accurate.
~D. Access to support can strengthen independent learning.#This is accurate.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q13::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Passage: A modern library is no longer only a storage place for printed books. Which revision improves academic style? Original: The library is not just a place with book stuff. {
~A. The library is not just book stuff and things.#This remains informal.
=B. The library is no longer only a place for printed books.#Correct. This improves academic style and clarity.
~C. The library has books and a bunch of other stuff.#This remains informal.
~D. The library is like not only a book place.#This is informal.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q14::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. Which analytical response is strongest? {
=A. The passage emphasizes balance because it values both texts and support services as parts of learning.#Correct. This analyzes the function of the idea.
~B. The passage says libraries have books.#This is true but too limited.
~C. The passage uses the word library.#This identifies a word, not analysis.
~D. The passage is easy to understand.#This does not analyze the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q15::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. Which sentence uses commas correctly in a series? {
~A. People attend workshops use technology meet with tutors and access study space.#Commas are missing.
=B. People attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access study space.#Correct. The series is punctuated clearly.
~C. People attend, workshops use, technology meet, with tutors.#The commas are misplaced.
~D. People, attend workshops, use technology meet with tutors, and access study space.#The first comma is incorrect and the series is unclear.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q16::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: This expanded role does not make books less important; instead, it shows that reading, research, and community learning now support one another. What must an accurate paraphrase preserve? {
=A. The idea that expanded library services support books and learning rather than replacing books#Correct. This preserves the relationship.
~B. The idea that books are no longer important#This contradicts the passage.
~C. The idea that research should stop#This contradicts the passage.
~D. The idea that community learning harms reading#This contradicts the passage.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q17::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Passage: When a library removes barriers to information and support, it strengthens independent learning. Which revision best improves clarity? Original: It helps them because they get it. {
~A. It really helps them because they totally get it.#This remains unclear.
=B. Access to information and support helps learners work more independently.#Correct. This identifies what helps and how.
~C. They get stuff and learn things.#This remains vague.
~D. It helps because it helps independent things.#This is circular.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q18::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. Which word best describes functions in this sentence? {
~A. Breaks#This is the opposite.
=B. Serves or operates#Correct. The library serves as a learning center.
~C. Stores secretly#This is unrelated.
~D. Questions#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q19::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A modern library is no longer only a storage place for printed books. In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. Which claim is too broad for the evidence? {
~A. Modern libraries may function as learning centers.#This is supported.
~B. Libraries can provide workshops, technology, tutoring, and study space.#This is supported.
=C. Every library in the world now provides the same services.#Correct. The passage says many communities, not every library.
~D. The passage expands the traditional view of libraries.#This is supported.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q20::[MLA.ENG4.L.01] Passage: A modern library is no longer only a storage place for printed books. Which sentence follows standard English conventions? {
~A. A modern library are no longer only a storage place.#The subject and verb do not agree.
=B. A modern library is no longer only a storage place.#Correct. The subject and verb agree.
~C. Modern library no longer only storage place.#This is not a complete standard sentence.
~D. A modern library, is no longer only a storage place.#The comma incorrectly separates subject and verb.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q21::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. Which revision best improves purpose? Original: There are things in libraries. {
~A. There are many things in many libraries.#This remains vague.
=B. Libraries support learning by providing texts, guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces.#Correct. This revision clarifies the purpose of the details.
~C. Libraries are places with stuff.#This is vague and informal.
~D. The library has some things, probably.#This weakens purpose and tone.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q22::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: When a library removes barriers to information and support, it strengthens independent learning. Which explanation best connects paraphrase to analysis? {
=A. The passage suggests access matters because reducing barriers helps people learn independently.#Correct. This paraphrases and explains function.
~B. Libraries have barriers, and barriers are things.#This is vague.
~C. Independent learning exists in the sentence.#This identifies wording without analysis.
~D. The passage is about support and information.#This is too general.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q23::[MLA.ENG4.V.01] Passage: A strong library program balances access to texts with access to guidance, tools, and collaborative spaces. What does access mean here? {
=A. The ability to use or reach something#Correct. Access means availability or ability to use.
~B. A claim with evidence#This is not the meaning.
~C. A spelling correction#This is unrelated.
~D. A private opinion#This is unrelated.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q24::[MLA.ENG4.W.04] Passage: This expanded role does not make books less important; instead, it shows that reading, research, and community learning now support one another. Which revision improves structure and style? Original: Books matter. Other stuff matters. It all works. {
~A. Books and other stuff matter and it all works.#This remains vague.
~B. Books matter because books are books and other things happen.#This is circular.
=C. Reading, research, and community learning support one another in the library's expanded role.#Correct. This is structured and academic.
~D. It all is important with stuff.#This is vague.
}
::ENG4_U01_L04_Q25::[MLA.ENG4.R.10] Passage: A modern library is no longer only a storage place for printed books. In many communities, the library functions as a learning center where people attend workshops, use technology, meet with tutors, and access quiet study space. Which analytical claim best fits the passage? {
=A. The passage changes the reader's understanding of libraries by emphasizing their role as active learning centers.#Correct. This is an analytical claim grounded in the passage.
~B. The passage proves books are outdated.#This contradicts the passage.
~C. The passage focuses only on technology.#This is too narrow.
~D. The passage argues that quiet study is the only useful library service.#This is too narrow.
}
